{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>For acceptance before YHWH.</b> One must know what idea these two words convey — that through them it will be 'for acceptance before YHWH.' Perhaps it intends, in saying <b>'holy'</b>, to refer to Israel, as it says (Jeremiah 2:3) ״קֹדֶשׁ יִשְׂרָאֵל,״ and the word <b>'to YHWH'</b> will further mean that the collectivity of Israel, so called, are holy to YHWH — desired, bound, and devoted. Therefore it will be <b>'for acceptance before YHWH'</b> — for He has desire toward Israel through the medium of the inscription, and this is the sod of (Song of Songs 6:3) ״אֲנִי לְדוֹדִי״ — and through this, ״וְדוֹדִי לִי״ (and my Beloved is for me)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:13.457987121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}